<Band Id="custom" Kicker="Custom agents">
    <h2 class="chrome reveal">Want an agent for your business? Louis builds them on this framework.</h2>
    <p class="lede reveal">An agent of your own is three things: who it is, the tools it uses on your own systems, and a closed place to run where every request is measured. Here is what each one holds, and Louis in the corner can pass your details on.</p>
    <div class="custom-grid">
        <TileRow Columns="1">
            <Tile Title="Your identity">Who the agent is for your business: its voice, its roles and the rules it keeps, written as files you can read and change.</Tile>
            <Tile Title="Your packs" Delay="1">Tools for your own systems, written once as a package: your data read in code, never guessed, with the engine's guards around every call.</Tile>
            <Tile Title="Hosted, closed and measured" Delay="2">Run for you in a closed Docker container that sees only what you hand it, in Azure's South African region if you want your data here, every request priced and the bill shown in rand. Checked by evals before anyone sees a change. <a href="/framework/how-it-works">The rules it keeps</a></Tile>
        </TileRow>
        <LiveTurn />
    </div>
    <p class="band-note"><strong>What we sell today:</strong> web hosting with an AI agent, for small businesses. Your website, hosted, with an agent in the corner like this one that knows your business and answers your customers. R500 to R1,000 a month, plus a once-off fee to build the site. <a href="/pricing">See the plans</a>.</p>
    <p class="band-note"><strong>Your first files, written with you:</strong> an agent is a few Markdown files, its voice, its roles and what it knows about your business. Louis can write your first Markdown files with you, for a fee, so your agent starts out sounding like you. <a href="/contact">Ask about it</a>.</p>
